ass=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Guess it's not like I need to worry about legal stuff, true.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like they'll be extremely excited and happy if you took their stuff and used it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T18:27:39-07:00","id":1340881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1331162-wip-exalted-distilled-reincarnated?p=1340604#post1340604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was mostly talking about Kyman's post, because it was the same sentiment I got every single time I tried to get any engagement or disussion going about ideas, people like them pop up.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ohohoho, I am so smart. Look at me, taking a bad faith argument about everything. Oh lookit me, I'm going to just insult and put down for no reason.&quot; It's not even mean criticism--there's nothing useful in that entire post! Just complaints and whining that I'm *creating something*.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for giving my genuine opinion when looking through your project. I may take a peek at the second draft, unless you'd rather I not because clearly my opinions aren't welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T18:40:31-07:00","id":1340884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1331162-wip-exalted-distilled-reincarnated?p=1340881#post1340881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry for giving my genuine opinion when looking through your project. I may take a peek at the second draft, unless you'd rather I not because clearly my opinions aren't welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're going to be like your original post....no, they really aren't welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T19:11:25-07:00","id":1340887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1331162-wip-exalted-distilled-reincarnated?p=1340884#post1340884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they're going to be like your original post....no, they really aren't welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck with your rework then. I do mean that sincerely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T19:11:54-07:00","id":1340888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1331162-wip-exalted-distilled-reincarnated?p=1340887#post1340887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good luck with your rework then. I do mean that sincerely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, and have fun with Exalted as it is. I also do mean that sincerely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T06:58:19-07:00","id":1340940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1331162-wip-exalted-distilled-reincarnated?p=1340870#post1340870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> I'm rewriting the entire system. Night Caste will still be cool, even without Wound Penalties. Maybe like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> here says.<br /> <br /> I'm not arguing that things like wound penalties are a bad idea, or I begrudge anything about them. It's just that:<br /> <br /> 1. They're not as essential as a thematic as they would be in say... WoD or Eclipse Phase.<br /> 2. It's just another thing to remember.<br /> 3. From what I've personally observed, it's literally the first mechanic people forget about. Often for entire sessions. (and they're never super thrilled to be reminded about it either.)<br /> <br /> So from a complexity/benefit analysis....yeah, no reason to keep it around. Not in a streamlining project. Not a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, your previous post suggested a greater antipathy to them. I also wanted to highlight that as one of the 5 Solar Castes, and thus part of the &quot;core&quot; game experience, the Night Caste were a very prominent subversion to the idea of Exalted as a game of epic escalating kung fu battles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T07:10:12-07:00","id":1340944,"title":"","content":"On the 'taking away of wound penalties'...<br /> <br /> I think it works. Exalted work on different rules from mortals. Different penalties from lacking a skill. No infection. Increased durability. What's wrong with making it so that they can push through pain that would cripple ordinary mortals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T07:42:30-07:00","id":1340947,"title":"","content":"If wound penalties are no longer part of the system then this isn't the ability of the Exalted to push through pain, it's the system making no distinction between unwounded and dying, it'd be down to the Storyteller to have Mortal NPCs react realistically to injury to create this distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T10:37:05-07:00","id":1340971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1331162-wip-exalted-distilled-reincarnated?p=1340940#post1340940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, your previous post suggested a greater antipathy to them. I also wanted to highlight that as one of the 5 Solar Castes, and thus part of the &amp;quot;core&amp;quot; game experience, the Night Caste were a very prominent subversion to the idea of Exalted as a game of epic escalating kung fu battles.</div> </div> </div> </div>.........what. I have not talked about Night Castes at all until you brought them up. Don't put words in my mouth. I have no problems with them at all.<br /> <br /> The only Exalts (or castes) I've brought up is Abyssals, which I'm completely on record of not liking consistently. I have plans for them.<br /> <br /> I'm not keeping Wound Penalties in my conversion. I really don't care what you think on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T12:08:34-07:00","id":1340980,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1331162-wip-exalted-distilled-reincarnated?p=1340971#post1340971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.........what. I have not talked about Night Castes at all until you brought them up. Don't put words in my mouth. I have no problems with them at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>To wound penalties. In the initial post you seemed at least partially motivated by the idea that Exalted isn't supposed to be gritty especially with talk of wound advantages.<br /> The Night Caste are often kind of gritty, embodying expertise in activiities that are at odds with how a lot of people view the setting, so it's useful to figure out where you stand with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't care what you think on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, good luck with your project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T12:24:08-07:00","id":1340985,"title":"","content":"I would tend to veer on the sides that if you're going for rules-lighter, I would guess wounds-penalties are OK to go. You can abstract them out such that, if a character wounded earlier in the scene rolls poorly, you can play that out as, guess that wound really hurts about right now, while if she rolls good, well, that's just her fightin' spirit and luck kicking in. YMMV.<br /> <br /> If an NPC is seriously wounded, then you could dock their QC a point of strength or something when they crop up later in a story, representing incomplete recovery, as a judgment call, without needing wound penalties a specific thing to track or worry about.<br /> <br /> Depending on how Dragonmystic wants to deal with poison mechanics and called shots, you could introduce the &quot;Death by a thousand cuts&quot; fighter through those, so there could be a systemic way to handle it without having to worry about additional obligatory mental burden of wound penalties in every fight where you don't necessarily care about that archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T13:33:44-07:00","id":1340996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1331162-wip-exalted-distilled-reincarnated?p=1340985#post1340985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would tend to veer on the sides that if you're going for rules-lighter, I would guess wounds-penalties are OK to go. You can abstract them out such that, if a character wounded earlier in the scene rolls poorly, you can play that out as, guess that wound really hurts about right now, while if she rolls good, well, that's just her fightin' spirit and luck kicking in. YMMV.<br /> <br /> If an NPC is seriously wounded, then you could dock their QC a point of strength or something when they crop up later in a story, representing incomplete recovery, as a judgment call, without needing wound penalties a specific thing to track or worry about.<br /> <br /> Depending on how Dragonmystic wants to deal with poison mechanics and called shots, you could introduce the &amp;quot;Death by a thousand cuts&amp;quot; fighter through those, so there could be a systemic way to handle it without having to worry about additional obligatory mental burden of wound penalties in every fight where you don't necessarily care about that archetype.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, there are neat ways to do wound penalties in a neat way. My argument, though, is that they aren't necessary to the genre of Exalted (wuxia) and so their inclusion isn't needed. So....just toss them.<br /> <br /> It's one of the aspects I feel pretty confident about, so it's going to be a pretty hard sell to make me put them back in.<br /> <br /> Poisons and other &quot;DoT's&quot; are an aspect I'm low-key dreading writing up. They tend to be notoriously bad and fiddly across the board.<br /> <br /> I need to get the core base combat rules fun, snappy before worrying about those sorts of mechanics, though.<br /> <br /> I'm probably not going to let called shots be a thing in normal combat. (behomoths are a different story)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T21:53:24-07:00","id":1341573,"title":"","content":"Alright. Finally had some to sit down and write up the second pass at Combat. That leaves Projects (which remains largely unchanged from the first pass, as it was untested) and the Social System.<br /> <br /> <b>To keep tally of what is done:</b><br /> The following is a bit...non-elegant in its word style. The document is better written, sorry. XD<br /> <br /> <br /> Basic mechanics, such as Ability rolls, stunting, Motes, etc. are written. (I do still have to define what the Abilities are, not that they are that different from 3e.)<ul><li>Abilities are now just a <i>expected selection</i> of Abilities. It's perfectly fine to invent/use new abilities and their charm trees. Like Cooking or something.</li> <li><i>Esoteric</i> Abilities are added. These are the supernatural things that humans can't normally learn. This is where Sorcery, Necromancy, Shapeshifting, and the Elemental Abilities are being moved to. You can express something like &quot;Intelliigence + Shapeshifting&quot; or &quot;Charisma + Fire&quot; for your rolls.<ul><li>Exalts will have their charms typically descend from their <i>Esoteric</i> Abilities, rather than the Natural Abilities. Solars are special in that their Charms are <i>directly</i> descended from natural abilities.</li> </ul></li> <li>Motes have been combined into one pool, and the Anima Banner (minimum) level is determined by what Power you are using. If a Power says &quot;Totemic&quot;, you'll be going totemic for it. It'll be defined in the header of every Power, along with Type and Keyword.</li> <li>The Great Curse is just a narrative thing. No mechanics. You just role-play it.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Combat</b><br /> Combat is intentionally simple. I've found that exception-based games, (Dominion, Magic: the Gathering) work best with a simple base that is expanded on with their individual powers--enough hooks and mechanical levers to attach to, but not so much that it becomes a shambling mess.<ul><li><b>Martial Art</b>s descend straight from Abilities, rather than a singular &quot;Martial Arts&quot; Ability. Sidesteps that whole nonsense.</li> <li>Everyone is required to take a<b> Martial Arts</b>-it defines how the combat values are calculated. This is mostly a psychological thing, to be honest-the &quot;base, free&quot; version is just the standard way of calculating values. However, it forces players to go &quot;Oh, I should pickup Nightingale style since I'm a performer&quot; and avoids the issue where non-combat characters are twiddling their thumbs in combat.</li> <li>You have Endurance, which is your Round &quot;Energy&quot;. You can shift it to empower effects, or use it as a defense booster.</li> <li>Motes are your Energy Pool for the Scene. For now, I'm not having a special regeneration during combat, unless it is proven necessary.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Every round, each character gets two Half-Actions to perform: Move, take cover, raise defenses, Use a simple charm/combo, etc. <b>Diminishing Returns</b> are the &quot;flurry penalty,&quot; to encourage a bit of diversity in actions. They tend to just be Endurance surcharges-nothing super punishing. You can't use two simple charms, though. Don't want to bog down turn order with that.<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b><br /> Charms are divided into <b>Trivial </b>(showing off) <b>Minor</b> (Helpful) and <b>Major</b> categories. <b>Major </b>Charms are just standard charms. They behave exactly as you expect. <b>Minor</b> Charms don't have to be bought with xp to be used, so long as you meet their minimum requirements. They're a bit more expensive in Motes, Endurance, and/or timing to balance that out.<br /> <br /> <b>Custom</b> Charms are greatly encouraged. I detail the process I use when creating/modifying charms, which I think is something that Exalted really should do in their books too.<br /> <br /> <b>Strife</b><br /> These are you limited-use points per story. You can use this to activate an extra-powerful Excellency for the scene. Or you can expend one to use a Major Charm you don't own (yet).<br /> <br /> I had a lot of fun writing up Exaltation-specific 'super-excellencies&quot;--or &quot;Strife Expressions&quot; as I have called them. They started pretty normal, but got more and more fun as I had less and less to work on. I particularly love the Infernal and Alchemical ones. Infernals cause <i>other people to botch</i> in what would otherwise be a glorious moment. Alchemicals shift into overdrive, boosting an Attribute at the cost of their other Attributes.<br /> <br /> They'll have to be balanced, of course. The Fae Folk one is either broken as anything, or completely useless.<br /> <br /> I might go back on the more normal ones (Solars) and find a new path for them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T21:23:35-07:00","id":1343534,"title":"","content":"<b>Combat Revision, again.</b><br /> <br /> Endurance wasn't working out. There was a very narrow window where it would mechanically work like I wanted it to, and even then people seemed more annoyed at &quot;regenerating hit points&quot; than seeing it as &quot;Ablative armor&quot; like I wanted it to be. Ah well.<br /> <br /> <br /> Took a step back and researched what other wuxia-style games do. A good point they made was that the combat should be opened up more and determined by player narrative actions, rather than tabletop wargame inspiring things. <a href=\"http://www.animaprimerpg.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Anima Prime</a>, in particular, had some very good inspiration. Honestly I grudgingly admit it alone could be a good Exalted substitute.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>General rundown:</b><br /> We're back to the two-phase attacks now. You <b>Gather</b> <i>Impulse Points</i> through taking an Attribute+Ability action of your choice, and then expend those points in a <b>Decisive</b> attack. So this means you could spend a few rounds gathering your inner essence (Stamina+Integrity), study the opponents footwork (Perception + Performance), make a feinting attack (Dexterity+Melee) and then launch your decisive, damaging attack.<br /> <br /> (There is a limit on how many points you can expend on raw dice for an attack.)<br /> <br /> [Note: &quot;Gathering&quot; and &quot;Impulse&quot; are working names. I don't want to use &quot;Withering&quot; because the actions don't wither anything anymore. &quot;Initiative&quot; I don't like because it means something very specific in almost every other game.]]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Depending on how much damage you deal, you can inflict secondary effects on the target character, such as forcing them to move, disrupting their gathered Impulse, or--yes--even wounding them. (It's not automatically tied to health levels, which was my biggest complaint and reason against them. Regardless, someone made a compelling argument.)<ul><li>Mostly cosmetic, but the main health track is called &quot;Endurance&quot;. It's a good word, and I think it represents how you can be knocked out of a fight with both physical and non-physical damage.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> That should bring the number of stats of a fight to remember down to:<ul><li>Initiative order (static value, mostly)</li> <li>Defense Value (DV ) (static, value)<ul><li>Some attacks may target or ignore certain defenses, like Evasion, Soak, and Parry. These are all still static</li> </ul></li> <li>Accuracy Limit (static, value)</li> <li>Base Damage (static, value)</li> <li>Endurance</li> <li>Motes</li> <li>Impulse</li> </ul><br /> The less non-static numbers flying around the better. Then again, if you get rid of too many stats and variable numbers, it stops being a game. Always a balancing act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T08:50:08-08:00","id":1347248,"title":"","content":"I'm very happy with how this new combat system is running. When I did a playtest, it was way more inventive and cinematic than the Endurance based one, and it makes me very happy.<br /> <br /> Some stats need to be adjusted, and I need to balance some antagonist stats higher, but that's all fine tuning. I'm finally at a point with the combat where I feel the core is actually working in speed, visuals, and mechanical granularity.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------<br /> Playtesting Example:<br /> <br /> V'neef Moldan, a Wood-Aspect Dragonblood, has entered into a Fae Castle that is protected by an Ice Giant (Worthy Foe) and Goblins (2x Lesser Foe Packs)<br /> <br /> V'neef is a combat-optimized character: his Archery, Dodge, and even Athletics are extremely high. His antagonists turned out to be tuned too low.<br /> <br /> Combat starts, and he goes in guns (bows?) blazing. He takes a Gathering action and strafes across the battlefield, firing at one of the Goblin packs. He rolls extremely well and his base damage is high enough to wipe that particular pack out immediately. (The Storyteller takes not of this and quietly raises the health of the other pack so it's a bit of a challenge for this playtest.)<br /> The Ice Golem takes a Gathering action and pounds the battlefield as a show of force.<br /> <br /> The remaining Goblin pack swarms V'neef. Lesser Foes do not gather impulse, but they may only make an attack once every X Rounds.<br /> <br /> V'neef, having gathered enough Impulse from his first, crazy-good roll, launches a decisive attack against the Ice Golem. He launches into the air and lands ontop of the Goblins heads as a Stunt, firing arrow after arrow at the Golem. For good measure, he also uses charms which ensare his arrows with invading barbed thorns, dealing extra damage should the arrows hit, which they do.<br /> The Ice Golem is not pleased, and uses its giant fists to swipe and smash V'neef. V'neef's Dodge is extremely good, but the Ice Giant rolls just enough and smashes his fist into V'neef's chest. He loses a few points of health.<br /> <br /> The Goblins attempt to attack V'neef who has been thrown off their head by the force of the fist, but even slightly winded they are no match for his Dodge as he dances across their heads.<br /> V'neef taks another gathering action, this time vaulting off the heads of the goblins and firing down at them. He rolls enough to deal them damage, but not enough to get a full decisive attack on his next round.<br /> <br /> The Ice Golem takes a special Gathering Action and forms an ice wall as cover so it can have a moments respite. This special action either makes Partial Cover, which raises its DV, or Full Cover, which makes it unattackable until countered. However, this special action gathers no Impulse. It rolls really well, and forms a complete, impenatrable ice sphere around itself.<br /> <br /> V'neef, ignoring the harmless Goblin packs, leaps up on top of the ice sphere. He ponders for a moment-if he was a Fire Dragonblood he could just cut through the ice. But then he has a brilliant idea: He pulls out his stringed intrument (he minors in performance) and says he will use a Strife Point to shatter the ice with a resonant frequency with a custom Major Charm.<br /> <br /> There is a short discussion with the Storyteller on whether this is even possible, who concedes that this is Exalted and this is completely in genre, but they have V'neef roll to determine if the cover partially or fully shatters. V'neef manages to completely shatter the ice sphere, and gathers Impulse from his Gathering-Strife Action.<br /> The Ice golem is suprised and fearful, so rushes backwards as its Gathering action, casting ice shards across the battlefield.<br /> <br /> The remaining Goblins are terrified and disband, fleeing away.<br /> <br /> V'neef lines up a Decisive shot, with concentration, and launches an arrow right into the ice golem's forehead, shattering its remaining health.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> This all took about 0.5-0.75 hour, including teaching the combat system. While the antagonists and health stats need to be raised just a bit, I am extremely happy with how it turned out.<br /> There didn't even need to be charms expended to have a really cool fight scene!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T08:15:48-08:00","id":1347688,"title":"","content":"Definitely, I'm fed up with the Storyteller system. Specifically its Attributes and Abilities, and how those relate to Castes/Aspects, and how Ability-based Charms ruin the game's attempt to evoke the Martial Arts genre.<br /> <br /> As long as most Exalted base their Charms on Abilities, and as long as Archery, Brawl, Melee, and Thrown remain Abilities on which Charms are based, and those are all somehow separate and distinct from &quot;Martial Arts&quot;, you're never going to have a proper Martial Arts game.<br /> <br /> The fact that <i>Exalted </i>is firmly a game designed around playing demigods also works against this. Only Exalted can learn Martial Arts Charms, and the system doesn't allow anything below the level of the Terrestrial Exalted, and there aren't enough Terrestrial Exalted in Creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> The &quot;Burn Legend&quot; shard does a much better job at modeling a martial arts game, because any combat technique is martial arts. Boxing and Wrestling are treated as equal styles compared to Eastern styles, and aren't rolled together into &quot;Brawl&quot; and then reskinned for each Ability-based Exalt.<br /> <br /> Also, anyone can learn the universal combat techniques, so it's fully possible to model someone who just barely knows how to fight and then gracefully scale upwards to someone who knows Everything about fighting. The entire spectrum is there for every level of challenge.<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible to generate an Okami beast-spirit warrior who is a paper tiger; a big and scary opponent who is so much worse at actually fighting that a purely mortal combatant can defeat him through superior kung fu. And then this mortal could fight progressively more skilled Okami, until he is powerless to defeat the Sage Beast Master without the help of his lifelong martial arts rival.<br /> <br /> <br /> But &quot;Burn Legend&quot; was a throw-away alternative which has received no more expansion. So I think I want to look into something like <i>Legends of Wulin, Weapons of the Gods</i>, or any other game that focuses more on &quot;kung fu&quot; and less on &quot;blessed by the gods&quot;.<br /> <br /> Adding the blessing of the gods to a kung fu game should be much easier than trying to build a mortal-accessible kung fu system within a game designed around playing demigods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-11-2019, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T09:01:10-08:00","id":1347696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1331162-wip-exalted-distilled-reincarnated?p=1347688#post1347688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely, I'm fed up with the Storyteller system. Specifically its Attributes and Abilities, and how those relate to Castes/Aspects, and how Ability-based Charms ruin the game's attempt to evoke the Martial Arts genre.<br /> <br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Martial Arts&quot;, for my design philosophy, is simply how the character interacts with combat. There are specific Styles and techniques, of course, just like there are specific charms and Powers. But you can always create your own.<br /> <br /> Mechanics: (subject to change)<br /> Specific Styles will be associated with whichever Ability closest represents them, and are just collections of similarly-themed and mechanically cohesive Powers. I want your Tiger Styles, Mantis styles, as well as your wacky and weird styles like in Read Or Die, where you can form a paper airplane and do a death by a thousand papercuts. (...bureaucracy? Probably Bureaucracy. Maybe Linquistics or Lore)<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Combat Abilities and their charms: they can simply be thought of &quot;general purpose&quot; Martial Arts Techniques---available regardless what sort of Martial Arts Style you have picked up. Techniques should be restricted to being in a specific form Style. (Note to self: add in mechanics for people who are dual/fusion stylists. Probably just a small xp charge to fuse two styles together. Or do I even need that restriction? Is just the charm/Technique choice fine enough?)<br /> <br /> <br /> Mortals should be able to learn almost all but the most esoteric Martial Arts. They will be restricted to Lesser Techniques, and will probably have a mote-like resource that can only be used for Lesser Techniques.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial and Mastery Keywords and their concepts are gone.<br /> <br /> Some specific Martial Art Styles will be tied with certain Esoteric Abilities-typically for self-explanatory reason. The Elemental Styles require being able to manipulate the elements, Prototype's Alex Mercer shoggothic body-horror style will need shapeshifting, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Does this sound along the lines of what you were thinking/wanting? Deficient in something that you wanted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T16:10:26-08:00","id":1350722,"title":"","content":"<b>Note:</b><u>I'm still looking for a co-writer, a partner in crime for this project.</u> It is admittedly exhausting doing this project on my own, and I would like the company. We could even just start up a discord group if we wanted to just idly chat, pull things apart, and put them back together.<br /> <br /> -----------------------<br /> <b>Social Encounters</b><br /> I've done work on making a Social Encounter system. To be clear, Social Encounters are very specific things: the Player Characters <i>want something to happen</i>. This is the system to enact change on the world, or bring about a consequence to happen. It's not the system to inspire, instill, or change people's minds--that can only be done through narrative means.<br /> <br /> You battle against the scene itself, gathering energy through platitudes, intimidation, motive gathering, etc. Then you spy onto Key Issues that are blocking your path, finding out their nature. Then, you must take action against that Key Issue, attempting to nullify its influence upon the scene--you assuage a fear of the Immaculate Order, you lay out precise maps of trade routes to strengthen your money-making scheme, or you intimidate sycophants.<br /> <br /> Once all Key Issues have been taken care of, you do a final Argument to tie everything together. If you have done well up to this point, this is simply a formality to see how well you succeed on your outcome. If you have not, it is the final attempt to pull successes from the jaws of defeat.<br /> <br /> Specific points I want to make about this subsystem:<br /> <br /> * All characters are active during the scene. The Socialiate will have more tools and tend to shine more in their element, but the big brute can stand around physically intimidating, smashing things. The Intellectual can draw and use their maps and diagrams as they please. It's a whole Party thing.<br /> * The scene, and not individuals, are what the Player Characters are struggling against. You could have the most weak willed character as your central antagonist--or no central antagonist at all--and still have a challenging scene.<br /> -----------------------<br /> Social Encounters seem to be working alright. I think it needs another iteration or two before it gets to its final form, though.<br /> <br /> -----------------------<br /> <b>Martial Arts</b><br /> <br /> I've started work on detailing out the specific Martial Arts, instead of simple nebulous ideas. Instead of simply translating the style over, I'm taking it apart and putting it back together with my reinterpretation of that. A big part of my rewrite is to just lessen the sheer number of charms/Techniques, so trying to pick and choose what abilities and themes are present is a challenge in itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Snake Style</b> turned out fun. I'm not a big fan of poison counters/DoT's as they slow down campaigns and turn order, but I think I've got a good compromise on that. I'll probably have to rewrite it by the time I've gone through all Martial Arts and Charms, since it'll probably be outdated by then.<br /> <br /> <b>Tiger Style</b> is proving to be a bit of tough nut to crack. I'm going to be honest, I don't think this Style is the best-written in 3e. Thematically, it's kinda all over the place--pouncing, extra damage, grapples, bonuses to attack/defense, maiming.... I'm going to just have to pick one or two themes and stick to them. I'm leaning to removing all the grapple/restrain themes and making those into a &quot;Bear&quot; style or something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}